WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:07.161
Hi. In this tutorial you will install ORIVEXY
Verify on Odoo.sh, step by step, and

2
00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:11.094
leave it working with a first
test validation.

3
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:16.587
Before you pay, ORIVEXY Verify checks that every
IBAN in your payment batch belongs

4
00:00:16.587 --> 00:00:21.623
to who it says. It cross-checks it with the
account ownership certificate your bank

5
00:00:21.623 --> 00:00:22.230
gives you.

6
00:00:22.683 --> 00:00:28.352
It tells you which payments are correct, which go
to someone else and which accounts

7
00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:33.617
are not in the certificate. Everything runs
inside your own Odoo: no bank data

8
00:00:33.617 --> 00:00:34.899
leaves your server.

9
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:40.676
Before you start you need three things: an
Odoo.sh project with administrator

10
00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:46.348
rights, access to the project's GitHub
repository, and ORIVEXY Verify purchased on

11
00:00:46.348 --> 00:00:50.014
Odoo Apps, for the same Odoo
version as your project.

12
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.162
Part two: preparation.

13
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:59.459
Find ORIVEXY Verify on Odoo Apps and choose
your Odoo version. It is a one-time

14
00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:05.671
payment per version. After the purchase, Odoo
Apps lets you download the module as a

15
00:01:05.671 --> 00:01:06.337
ZIP file.

16
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:13.715
Inside the ZIP there is a folder,
orivexy_validator, which is the module. Inside it,

17
00:01:13.715 --> 00:01:18.831
the requirements.txt file lists the
Python libraries it needs.

18
00:01:19.283 --> 00:01:26.232
Your Odoo.sh project keeps its modules in a
GitHub repository. If you don't have a

19
00:01:26.232 --> 00:01:30.299
project yet, go to odoo.sh and
press Create New.

20
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.988
There you choose the repository, the Odoo
version and your Odoo Enterprise

21
00:01:35.988 --> 00:01:41.862
subscription code, and press Deploy. If you
already have a project, skip this step.

22
00:01:42.317 --> 00:01:47.153
Now, in a copy of the repository, create
a test branch and copy the

23
00:01:47.153 --> 00:01:51.845
orivexy_validator folder to the root,
next to your other modules.

24
00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:58.307
Add its libraries to the repository's
requirements.txt, the one Odoo.sh reads, and

25
00:01:58.307 --> 00:02:04.477
push the branch to GitHub. If you don't use the
terminal, you can do the same on the

26
00:02:04.477 --> 00:02:05.579
GitHub website.

27
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:08.777
Part three: installation.

28
00:02:09.217 --> 00:02:16.276
In your Odoo.sh project, open the Branches tab:
the new branch shows up on its own.

29
00:02:16.276 --> 00:02:23.250
Drag it to Staging. Odoo.sh will copy your
database and build the branch, with the

30
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.801
libraries in requirements.txt.

31
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:33.659
When the build is green, press Connect to open
the test database. From here on, what

32
00:02:33.659 --> 00:02:36.570
you see is real Odoo, version 18.

33
00:02:37.017 --> 00:02:44.289
First, activate developer mode. Open the
apps menu and go to Settings.

34
00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:49.478
Scroll to the bottom of the page and press
Activate the developer mode.

35
00:02:52.083 --> 00:02:59.094
Now go to Apps and press Update Apps List, so
Odoo finds the modules in the new

36
00:02:59.094 --> 00:02:59.715
branch.

37
00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:03.150
Type ORIVEXY in the search box.

38
00:03:03.617 --> 00:03:10.529
There is ORIVEXY Verify. Press Activate and
wait a few seconds while it installs.

39
00:03:10.983 --> 00:03:18.138
When it finishes, Odoo reloads the page.
ORIVEXY Verify now appears in the apps

40
00:03:18.138 --> 00:03:18.591
menu.

41
00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.194
Part four: initial setup.

42
00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:28.718
ORIVEXY Verify works as soon as it is installed;
you only decide who sees what. Each

43
00:03:28.718 --> 00:03:34.207
internal user sees their own validations. A
manager sees everyone's in their

44
00:03:34.207 --> 00:03:37.458
company, without being an
Odoo administrator.

45
00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:44.244
To make someone a manager, go to Settings,
Users and Companies, Users, and open

46
00:03:44.244 --> 00:03:45.285
their record.

47
00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:52.926
With developer mode on, under Access Rights tick
ORIVEXY Verify: Manager, and save.

48
00:03:53.383 --> 00:03:58.418
If you work with several companies, each
validation is stored in its own company,

49
00:03:58.418 --> 00:04:02.335
and each user only sees those of the
companies they can access.

50
00:04:02.783 --> 00:04:07.833
There is no licence to activate: the one-time
Odoo Apps payment covers the module

51
00:04:07.833 --> 00:04:13.071
and the desktop app. There are no integrations to
set up either, because it does not

52
00:04:13.071 --> 00:04:14.879
connect to external services.

53
00:04:15.317 --> 00:04:22.406
One detail: scanned certificates need text
recognition, which Odoo.sh does not

54
00:04:22.406 --> 00:04:29.405
include. For those, use the bank's text PDF,
the SEPA XML or the desktop app.

55
00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:34.999
The desktop app is downloaded from the module
itself, under ORIVEXY Verify, Desktop

56
00:04:34.999 --> 00:04:38.970
app, for anyone who prefers to work
with the files outside Odoo.

57
00:04:39.417 --> 00:04:43.977
Part five: a test validation,
with fictitious data.

58
00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:52.329
Open ORIVEXY Verify. Validations will list all
your checks; the first time, the list

59
00:04:52.329 --> 00:04:53.177
is empty.

60
00:04:53.617 --> 00:05:01.172
Press New. Under Certificate, upload the bank's
account ownership certificate, as a

61
00:05:01.172 --> 00:05:08.545
PDF or SEPA XML. Under File to check, upload
your payment batch: TXT, CSV or XML.

62
00:05:08.983 --> 00:05:14.935
Press VALIDATE. In a couple of seconds you
have the result for every payment.

63
00:05:15.383 --> 00:05:20.830
At the top is the summary: nine payments, six
correct, two in another holder's name

64
00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:23.783
and one whose IBAN is not in
the certificate.

65
00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:29.532
Below, each row shows the holder in your batch,
the one in the certificate and the

66
00:05:29.532 --> 00:05:31.786
result, with a note explaining why.

67
00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:37.137
Look at the payment to Pedro Fernández: the
IBAN is in the certificate, but it

68
00:05:37.137 --> 00:05:42.212
belongs to María López. That payment should not
go out without confirming it with

69
00:05:42.212 --> 00:05:43.026
the supplier.

70
00:05:43.483 --> 00:05:48.019
With View discrepancies you keep
only what needs attention.

71
00:05:48.483 --> 00:05:54.658
Open a row and press Start review. Write what
you checked and resolve it: the note

72
00:05:54.658 --> 00:05:58.875
is required and is recorded with
your name and the date.

73
00:05:59.683 --> 00:06:06.720
From the validation you can print the PDF
report, with masked IBANs, or export the

74
00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.779
results to Excel or CSV.

75
00:06:09.217 --> 00:06:16.896
This is how to read the results. Correct:
nothing to do. Wrong holder: hold the

76
00:06:16.896 --> 00:06:22.825
payment and check it. Manual review:
you decide, with a note.

77
00:06:23.283 --> 00:06:29.990
IBAN not found: its certificate is missing.
And invalid IBAN: the number is

78
00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:30.795
mistyped.

79
00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:34.274
Part six: final check.

80
00:06:34.717 --> 00:06:39.942
The installation is complete if ORIVEXY
Verify appears in the menu, a test

81
00:06:39.942 --> 00:06:45.661
validation ends with results, and a regular
user only sees their own validations.

82
00:06:46.117 --> 00:06:51.996
The most common errors are quick to fix. If it
does not appear in Apps, check that

83
00:06:51.996 --> 00:06:57.731
the folder is at the root of the branch and
update the list. If the build fails,

84
00:06:57.731 --> 00:07:02.965
look at its logs: it is almost always a
missing line in requirements.txt.

85
00:07:03.417 --> 00:07:08.965
If a certificate cannot be read, it is probably
a scanned image. And if a manager

86
00:07:08.965 --> 00:07:14.649
cannot see other people's validations, check
their access right on the user record.

87
00:07:15.083 --> 00:07:20.812
Always test in Staging. When everything is
right, merge the branch into production

88
00:07:20.812 --> 00:07:25.283
and, in that database, install the
module just as you have seen.

89
00:07:25.717 --> 00:07:31.387
To update to a new version, replace the folder
with the one from the new ZIP, push

90
00:07:31.387 --> 00:07:34.429
the change and upgrade the
module from Apps.

91
00:07:34.883 --> 00:07:41.976
And that's it: ORIVEXY Verify installed and
working on Odoo.sh. If you need help,

92
00:07:41.976 --> 00:07:47.843
write to us from the module page on Odoo
Apps. Thanks for watching.
